Running ACPI20030918 on linux 2.4.22

At least the battery is not properly detected. It is seen as "present"
when it is not.

Attached files (names are self-explainatory):
dmesg-s40000
dmidecode
acpidmp
lspci-vv
interrupts

Here is what /proc/acpi/battery/BAT1/info says when battery in not plugged:
present:                 yes
design capacity:         5400 mAh
last full capacity:      5400 mAh
battery technology:      rechargeable
design voltage:          8191 mV
design capacity warning: 540 mAh
design capacity low:     162 mAh
capacity granularity 1:  264 mAh
capacity granularity 2:  3780 mAh
model number:            LIP9071
serial number:
battery type:            LiON
OEM info:                HP

File contains exactly the same things when battery is plugged.

(there is no such thing as a /proc/battery/BAT0/ directory here)

Buttons seem to be properly detected (power button, sleep button, lid button)

No fan is detected either, and no thermal information is given. (Might
this be because my laptop plainly doesn't support those features? This
laptop probably started being sold around end of 2001- This is HP Pavilion
N5422)

I will be pleased to send you any other information that could be
relevant, if that can help.

Please reply to me directly, as I am not subscribed to any ACPI-related
mailing list.

Thanks for the good work,

Vincent
